              "text": "Glucocorticoids—not recommended since drug use. do not alter course of the disease.",
              "pdf_page": 1506,
              "printed_page": 1424,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Trauma—overzealous ear flushing; usually",
              "pdf_page": 1506,
              "printed_page": 1424,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Antibiotics—recommended if otitis media occurs when cleaning performed under and interna cannot be ruled out; general anesthesia or sedation; signs follow trimethoprim-sulfa 15 mg/kg PO q12h; immediately upon recovery from anesthesia/first-generation cephalosporin (e.g., sedation. cephalexin 15–20 mg/kg PO q12h); drug of",
              "pdf_page": 1506,
              "printed_page": 1424,
              "column": 2
            }
          ]
        },
